course: dictionary
lesson: 4898
title: Prefixes and the word illegal
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A prefix is a small group of letters added to the front of a word to change its meaning. In «illegal», the prefix is il-, and it means not. Legal means allowed by the law, so illegal means not allowed by the law.
explain: The first letter of the root word often tells you which prefix to use. Il- goes before l, as in illegal and illogical. Im- goes before m or p (impossible), ir- goes before r (irregular), and un- goes before many common words (unkind).
explain: «Getting into a computer or account without permission is illegal in most countries.» Here illegal means against the law. Check it by swapping in «not allowed by the law»: the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Illegal also has a meaning in games. «An illegal move» in chess breaks the rules of the game. It is the same idea as the law, just for a game instead of a country.
fact: A prefix is a group of letters added to the start of a word to change its meaning.
fact: The prefix il- means not, so «illegal» means not legal.
fact: Illegal means against the law of a country, and the police can act against illegal things.
fact: In games, «illegal» means against the rules, as in «an illegal move».
fact: Other prefixes that mean not include un- (unkind), in- (incorrect), im- (impossible) and ir- (irregular).
exercise: «Getting into a computer without permission is illegal.» What does illegal mean here? | Made of glass | Full of colour | *Against the law | Very quick
exercise: What does the prefix il- mean in «illegal»? | Under | *Not | Very big | Again
exercise: Which prefix goes before «logical» to make a word meaning not logical? | *il- | im- | un- | ir-
test: In a game, what does «an illegal move» mean? | *A move against the rules | A move made very quickly | A move made by the referee | A move that wins the game
test: What is the opposite of «legal»? | Local | Lawful | Loyal | *Illegal
exam: «Stealing is illegal.» What can the police do about it? | *Act against it | Give a prize | Say sorry | Close the shop
